# Backtest Plan — Priority 1

**Drafted 6 September 2026 · for execution week of 8 September**

---

## 1. Why this is priority one

Every result produced so far rests on **49 weekly rebalances in a single market episode**.
That episode turned out to be more useful than assumed — it contains a −14.8% drawdown and
21 RISK-OFF weeks — but it is still one episode. Nothing has been validated across a second
independent period.

Specifically unvalidated:

| Item | Current evidence | Needed |
|---|---|---|
| Expectancy in R | never measured | walk-forward, out-of-sample |
| Drawdown distribution | one observed path | Monte Carlo, 10,000 reshuffles |
| Parameter settings | single-point tests on 49 weeks | plateau at ±30% |
| 2:1 reward:risk floor | untested | plateau |
| 12% stop cap | untested | plateau |
| 2-week hysteresis | untested | plateau |
| Regime thresholds (45 / 65) | one correction, worked well | second episode |
| SMS weights 30/20/20/15/10/5 | never varied | plateau |

The regime layer is the one component with genuine evidence behind it: it cut deployment
60% → 30% on 16 Jan 2026 at a −3.2% drawdown, ahead of a further 10.5% decline, and stayed
defensive until 19 June. That behaviour needs confirming on a second drawdown, not
discovering for the first time.

