## 2. Data to fetch

**Target: January 2021.** Gives 4.7 tradeable years after the 252-session warm-up, and
includes the 2022 rotation-driven bear market — the specific condition this system has
never faced.

| Option | New sessions | Size | Tradeable years | Includes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Jan 2021 (recommended)** | ~936 | ~234 MB | **4.7** | 2022 bear, Oct 2024 correction |
| Jan 2020 | ~1,189 | ~297 MB | 5.7 | + COVID crash |
| Jan 2019 | ~1,441 | ~360 MB | 6.7 | + 2019 NBFC stress |

Jan 2020 is tempting for the COVID crash, but March 2020 was a liquidity event rather than a
rotation, and it would dominate any drawdown statistic. **Start with Jan 2021; extend later
if the walk-forward wants more in-sample years.**

### Command

```
python scripts/fetch_nse.py --backfill 2100
```

or Actions tab → Run workflow → backfill = `2100`.

Fetches both `data/sec_bhavdata_full_*.csv` and `indices/ind_close_all_*.csv`. Skips
existing files, so it is safe to re-run.

### Expectations

- **Slow.** The fetch is rate-limited and polite. Expect a long run and possible timeouts.
- **Gaps are normal.** Re-run the same command; it only fetches what is missing.
- **Verify before building.** Session count should land near 1,431. A shortfall of more than
  ~20 means gaps worth investigating rather than ignoring.

