## 5. What this will and will not settle

### Will settle

- Whether the rule set has out-of-sample expectancy
- Realistic drawdown distribution for position sizing
- Which parameters sit on plateaus and which are fitted
- Whether the regime gate generalises beyond one correct call
- The value of the regime and sector layers, measured rather than argued

### Will not settle

**v1 vs v2.** Both maps are current snapshots. Running either against 2022 gives the map
four years of hindsight about index membership. Constituent snapshots only began accumulating
on 4 Sep 2026.

That question stays with `state/map_comparison.jsonl` accumulating forward, where there is no
look-ahead. Decision gate remains 80 matured 4-week observations; currently 45.

**Gate-related selection.** G3–G8 are not modelled, so the backtest omits trades those gates
would have blocked. Per the protocol, live should beat backtest on gate-related names — if it
does not, something else is wrong.

